firming the app serves HTTP 200 in enforcing mode. Completed the mandatory single-node restart evidence protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id/enforcing/service state, restarted node1 with shutdown -r now, confirmed a new boot_id and reset uptime after reconnecting, and verified enforcing mode, httpd, the port policy, and the inventory app all recovered post-restart with no new AVC denials.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Checked baseline OS/SELinux/network state on node1 (RHEL 7.9, SELinux enforcing, no httpd/semanage installed)\",\"Enabled temporary CentOS 7 vault repos and installed httpd + policycoreutils-python (provides semanage)\",\"Created /var/www/inventory/index.html inventory app content and /etc/httpd/conf.d/inventory.conf listening on port 8181\",\"Started httpd before the SELinux port fix and captured the resulting bind failure and AVC name_bind denial (port 8181 was intermapper_port_t)\",\"Reassigned SELinux port context: semanage port -m -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181\",\"Restarted httpd, confirmed SELinux still Enforcing, and verified curl to $NODE_IP:8181 returns HTTP 200 with inventory content\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline: boot_id, uptime, getenforce, httpd active/enabled, curl 200, semanage port listing\",\"Issued a native reboot (shutdown -r now) via a backgrounded sudo command so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned, confirming a fresh uptime\",\"Captured post-restart evidence: new boot_id differing from baseline, getenforce Enforcing, httpd active, curl 200 with correct inventory content, semanage port context persisted, no new AVC denials for port 8181\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Inventory application served on TCP 8181 on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6450ea3d2e2945e4\",\"cmd-2a928964c6914d5f\",\"cmd-7f41a12bbc784b18\"],\"summary\":\"Created /var/www/inventory content and Apache vhost listening on 8181; httpd active and listening on :::8181; curl to $NODE_IP:8181 returns HTTP 200 with the inventory page content\"},{\"requirement\":\"SELinux mandatory access control remains in enforcing mode throughout\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-88322bcb4ea2432a\",\"cmd-69b7a24a7fc64bf0\",\"cmd-7f41a12bbc784b18\",\"cmd-5fd00b4564594ca1\"],\"summary\":\"getenforce consistently reports Enforcing before, during, and after configuring the service; /etc/selinux/config also set to enforcing\"},{\"requirement\":\"Fix is a genuine SELinux policy change, proven necessary (falsify-before-commit)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b18921fc50784845\",\"cmd-d630aadabca54297\",\"cmd-17debe1de5874062\",\"cmd-be12da3b70394933\"],\"summary\":\"httpd failed to bind 8181 with Permission denied and an AVC name_bind denial (tcontext=intermapper_port_t) before the fix; semanage port -m -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181 relabeled the port, after which httpd bound successfully\"},{\"requirement\":\"Pre-restart healthy baseline on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5fd00b4564594ca1\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 0d6209e2-350d-4cd9-8a7d-11f7c08072be, uptime, Enforcing, httpd active+enabled, curl 200, and semanage port listing showing http_port_t includes 8181\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection; single node restarted\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9c8d7ed218c24f2b\"],\"summary\":\"sudo shutdown -r now issued via backgrounded nohup so the ack/exit returned before the SSH-like session dropped (exit_code 255 with 'Connection closed by remote host' confirms the disconnect happened after acknowledgement)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node polled until command execution available again\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1b6aedda9a484be2\"],\"summary\":\"First successful exec after reboot shows 'up 0 min', confirming the node had just booted and exec access was restored\"},{\"requirement\":\"Changed boot identity proven (not just elapsed time or service state)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ee0de44047f6405d\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id is 1ea5f52c-39a9-4592-80f9-1a8aaa956274, differing from the pre-restart boot_id 0d6209e2-350d-4cd9-8a7d-11f7c08072be, with uptime reset to ~12s\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of required services/data/config verified\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ee0de44047f6405d\"],\"summary\":\"After restart: getenforce Enforcing, httpd active, curl to $NODE_IP:8181 returns HTTP 200 with correct inventory content, semanage port 8181 still mapped to http_port_t, and no new AVC denials for port 8181 since the new boot\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to serve the inventory application via Apache httpd on TCP 8181 while SELinux stayed in Enforcing mode, by relabeling the port's SELinux type from intermapper_port_t to http_port_t (semanage port -m -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181) rather than lowering MAC enforcement. Verified the fix was necessary by first reproducing an AVC name_bind denial, then confirming the app serves HTTP 200 in enforcing mode. Completed the mandatory single-node restart evidence protocol: captured pre-restart boot_id/enforcing/service state, restarted node1 with shutdown -r now, confirmed a new boot_id and reset uptime after reconnecting, and verified enforcing mode, httpd, the port policy, and the inventory app all recovered post-restart with no new AVC denials.","actions_performed":["Checked baseline OS/SELinux/network state on node1 (RHEL 7.9, SELinux enforcing, no httpd/semanage installed)","Enabled temporary CentOS 7 vault repos and installed httpd + policycoreutils-python (provides semanage)","Created /var/www/inventory/index.html inventory app content and /etc/httpd/conf.d/inventory.conf listening on port 8181","Started httpd before the SELinux port fix and captured the resulting bind failure and AVC name_bind denial (port 8181 was intermapper_port_t)","Reassigned SELinux port context: semanage port -m -t http_port_t -p tcp 8181","Restarted httpd, confirmed SELinux still Enforcing, and verified curl to $NODE_IP:8181 returns HTTP 200 with inventory content","Captured